From: ggbdpq <ggbdpq@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:08:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(gateway): translated requests keep the caller's
 correlation carriers (#4899)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed
A provider configured by its URL alone speaks Chat Completions, so an
Anthropic Messages or an OpenAI Responses request is translated for it —
and the caller's correlation carriers never reached it: the body's
metadata object, the X-Cid header and the URL's query string were all
dropped on the way, which left a caller unable to pair its turns with
what the provider served (yetone/magpie#4899).

- The translation carries the caller's metadata on: an Anthropic
  client's metadata went into the request it is built again from, and
  a Responses client's is read beside its client_metadata now, so the
  built Chat request has it as it was sent. An upstream that turns the
  field away by name is asked again without it, and is not sent it
  again, as the cache key already is.
- The caller's X-Cid header goes on every request to the provider,
  translated or relayed, the user's own header for the provider still
  replacing it in the signing.
- The caller's query string rides the path a translated request goes
  by, the path's own parameters (Code Assist's alt=sse) standing, and
  no parameter a caller's credential travels by with it: a gateway key
  comes in the query (Gemini's clients), and a caller's key is
  magpie's, never the provider's.

Run
go test -tags nogui -count=1 ./internal/gateway/ (the one red,
TestCodexPoolSaysTheClientsVersion, went red in the full-suite run and
is green alone and at -count=3 on both this branch and the parent
commit: a known full-suite flake, not this change)
go test -tags nogui -count=1 ./internal/... (TestHostToldTheGatewayAddress
in internal/plugin is red on the parent commit too)
go vet, gofmt, GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build, GOOS=windows
GOARCH=amd64 go build, go build on darwin.

